<p>Base class <b>generated</b> by <code>make_text_icons.py</code> (folder tools/ of the repository) - do not edit by hand: change the script and run it again. Icon of a 4-line, 32-column text screen: cell <code>k</code> shows the character whose ASCII code is <code>textCode[k]</code>, line <code>i</code>, column <code>j</code> being <code>k = (i - 1)*32 + j</code>. It extends <code>Internal.PartialTextDisplay</code>, which declares the array and fills it: the names of a <code>DynamicSelect</code> are resolved in the class that carries the icon, so the array must be in scope here (declared by a sibling base class, it is not found and the screen stays empty in replay).</p>
<p>Same technique as <code>Internal.TwoLineTextIcon</code> (a <code>String</code> is not stored in the results, an <code>Integer</code> is) and same tolerant comparison (<code>abs(code - N) &lt; 0.5</code>, robust to the interpolation of the replay). Character set: space, digits, letters and <code>! &quot; # &amp; &apos; ( ) * + , - . / : &lt; = &gt; ? _</code>; any other character is shown as a space.</p>
</html>"));
